Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat(client):=20transcript=20extension=20seams?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20=E2=80=94=20user-body=20chain=20and=20prose=20inline=20direc?=
 =?UTF-8?q?tives?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two generic seams for features that encode structure into sent text or
expect structure back in answers:

- conversation.chat.user-body: chain slot dispatched for every user
  bubble body (durable and pending steering); currency is the sent text
  alone, all-decline falls through to the plain projection. The
  annotation-specific parsing MessageItem carried moves out to its owner.
- MarkdownInlineDirectives: the markdown renderer resolves
  :name{key="value"} prose runs through an owner vocabulary reached via
  the optional chatInlineDirectives service (lazy per directive, one
  stable delegate); unresolved runs stay literal, settled renders only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
